## Fix 1 — Race condition on navigate-away during inference (H1)

In result.tsx, the run() function is async and fires inside a useEffect. If
the user navigates away (back button, switching food type, etc.) before
analyzePhoto/persistPhoto/saveResult finish, the component may already be
unmounted, causing state updates on an unmounted component.

Fix:
1. Add a ref: const isCancelled = useRef(false)
2. In the useEffect's cleanup function, set isCancelled.current = true
3. After EVERY await inside run() (after analyzePhoto, after persistPhoto,
   after saveResult, and any other async step in that function), check
   `if (isCancelled.current) return;` before calling any setState/setPhase.
4. Show me the full updated run() function so I can review every await is
   covered, not just the first one.

